Lab 14: Importing Virtual Machines
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Import virtual machines from external hypervisors using the Open Virtual Appliance (OVA) format
Configure network and storage options for imported VMs in OpenShift Virtualization
Verify VM functionality after successful import
Understand the migration process from traditional virtualization platforms to OpenShift Virtualization
Troubleshoot common import issues and validate VM performance
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of virtualization concepts
Familiarity with OpenShift Virtualization fundamentals
Knowledge of Linux command-line operations
Understanding of networking concepts (IP addressing, VLANs)
Basic knowledge of storage concepts in virtualization environments
Access to OpenShift cluster with Virtualization operator installed
Lab Environment
Ready-to-Use Cloud Machines: Al Nafi provides pre-configured Linux-based cloud machines with OpenShift Virtualization already set up. Simply click Start Lab to begin - no need to build your own VM or install additional software.

Your lab environment includes:

OpenShift cluster with Virtualization operator
